### wayfinder sweep caches
# source-trees.json is 3.9 MB of GitHub path listings, cheap to refetch.
# board-scan.json is NOT ignored: it holds every footprint name the corpus
# places, which is what makes the next lexicon question answerable without
# re-reading 600 MB of board files. Its predicate has been wrong twice.
data/source-trees.json
data/board-sizes.json
# Every README in the corpus, whole: the input to draft_summaries.py, refilled by
# measure_summaries.py. Other people's text, so never committed.
data/readme-scan.json

# Claude Code worktrees -- scratch checkouts, never part of the tree.
.claude/worktrees/

# Board files generated from a repo's Ergogen config -- a cache generate_ergogen.py refills.
data/generated-boards/

# The dev OAuth app secret for a real GitHub sign-in under bootRun (#116).
github-dev.env

### Private, on the owner's machine only
# Working notes, the backlog, design docs and drafts. Never part of the public repo.
.scratch/
docs/design/
docs/research/affiliate-programs.md
docs/research/parts-picker-ux.md
# The owner's AI-assistant setup and skills (some vendored from others' repos).
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json
.termdbms/
